  "result": "Perfect! All 366 tests pass \u2713\n\n**Added dashboard(invoices, asOf) to src/reports.js:**\n\nReturns a comprehensive summary object with:\n\n1. **counts** - Number of invoices per status\n   - draft, issued, partially_paid, paid\n\n2. **outstanding** - Total amount still due on issued/partially_paid invoices\n   - Excludes draft and paid invoices\n   - Uses balanceDue() for accuracy\n\n3. **overdue** - Object with count and amount\n   - count: number of overdue invoices\n   - amount: total amount overdue\n   - Derived from overdueInvoices() function\n\n4. **topCustomers** - Top 3 customers with most outstanding amount\n   - Format: [{ customerId, due }, ...]\n   - Sorted highest amount first\n   - Limited to 3 results\n   - Only includes customers with outstanding balance > 0\n   - Sums multiple invoices per customer\n\n**Example output:**\n```javascript\n{\n  counts: { draft: 0, issued: 3, partially_paid: 0, paid: 0 },\n  outstanding: 28919,  // \u20ac289.19\n  overdue: { count: 3, amount: 28919 },\n  topCustomers: [\n    { customerId: 'C-001', due: 22990 },\n    { customerId: 'C-002', due: 5929 }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n**Added 19 comprehensive tests** covering:\n- Empty invoices list\n- Invoice counting by status\n- Outstanding calculation (issued/partially_paid)\n- Exclusion of draft and paid from outstanding\n- Overdue count and amount\n- Top customers sorting and limits\n- Multiple invoices per customer aggregation\n- Structure validation\n- Data type validation (integers)\n- Edge cases and boundary conditions",
